en.math:
\begin{aligned}
\ddot a R
&=-\frac{G}{d^2}\left(\frac{4\pi}{3}\rho d^3\right) \\
&=-\frac{4\pi G}{3}\rho d \\
&=-\frac{4\pi G}{3}\rho aR.\end{aligned}

p.src:
The galaxy’s physical speed is $\dot d=\dot a R$, and its distance from the chosen origin is $d=aR$. Its conserved Newtonian energy is therefore $\boxed{
E=\frac12 m\dot a^{\,2}R^2-\frac{GMm}{aR}.
}$

